course: dictionary
lesson: 11345
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a place or a history, and you need the context to know which meaning is meant. «China was ruled by dynasties, families whose rule passed from parent to child, such as the Shang, Zhou, Qin, Han, Tang, Song and Ming.» Here Zhou is the name of a dynasty, a royal family and its time. The sentence tells you what it means.
explain: Zhou can also be a surname, a family name like Smith or Patel. Read the words around it: a dynasty, a ruler, or a person called Zhou Enlai. The capital letter is a clue too, because names start with one. A Mandarin word zhōu would only fit if the sentence were about Chinese words, not about history or people.
explain: «Later the Zhou kings said Heaven gave a just ruler the right to rule.» Words like kings and ruler show that Zhou is a royal family. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Zhou is a name, so it begins with a capital letter.
fact: The Zhou dynasty ruled China for about 800 years, from about 1046 BC to 256 BC.
fact: The Zhou dynasty is the time of Confucius and the idea of the Mandate of Heaven.
fact: Zhou is also a common Chinese surname, as in Zhou Enlai, a Chinese premier.
fact: In Mandarin, zhōu is a different word that can mean porridge, state or province; it is not an English word.
exercise: «The Zhou dynasty ruled China for about 800 years.» How long did the Zhou dynasty rule? | *About 800 years | About 8000 years | About 8 years | About 80 years
exercise: Zhou is a common Chinese surname. What kind of word is Zhou here? | A type of porridge | A word for a week | A type of weather | *A name
exercise: «The Zhou dynasty is the time of Confucius.» Which word tells you Zhou is a time in history? | *dynasty | Confucius | time | is
test: In Mandarin, zhōu can mean porridge. Why is it not the same as the name Zhou? | *It is a different word in another language, and the sentence tells you which one | It is spelled differently in English | It is always about history | It is the same word in every sentence
test: «Later the Zhou kings said Heaven gave a just ruler the right to rule.» What kind of people were the Zhou kings? | People who sold porridge | Teachers who wrote books | Rebels who fought the ruler | *A royal family who ruled
exam: Jayden sees «Zhou» in a history book and in a Chinese cookbook about porridge. How can he tell which meaning is which? | Guess, since the spelling is always the same | Look up every word, since context never helps | *Look at the words around it and the capital letter, and check which meaning fits the sentence
